<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Antoine de Lamothe Cadillac</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1658–1730</span> · <a href="/centuries/18th-century">18th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Antoine de Lamothe Cadillac was a French adventurer and colonial officer in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/north-america">North America</a>. After commanding the post at Michilimackinac, he founded Fort Pontchartrain du Détroit on the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/detroit">Detroit</a> River in 1701, the origin of the city of Detroit. He was later governor of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/louisiana">Louisiana</a>, from 1710 to 1716.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/antoine-de-lamothe-cadillac.jpg" alt="Antoine de Lamothe Cadillac" width="215" height="274" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: op unknown · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Antoine_de_la_Mothe_Cadillac.JPG" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
